WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.950
Help is on the way.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:05.200
Now your job is to make the rescue easy.

3
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:08.575
Follow the rescuers’ instructions exactly.

4
00:00:08.825 --> 00:00:12.400
They may ask you to hold a particular course and speed.

5
00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.025
Do it, even if it seems odd.

6
00:00:15.275 --> 00:00:20.900
Before a helicopter arrives, secure everything loose: gear, canvas, antennas.

7
00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.825
The rotor wash is like a hurricane.

8
00:00:24.075 --> 00:00:27.575
When they lower the basket or the hook, don’t reach for it.

9
00:00:27.825 --> 00:00:30.475
Let it touch the water or the deck first.

10
00:00:30.725 --> 00:00:31.975
Why?

11
00:00:32.975 --> 00:00:40.725
A hovering helicopter builds up a powerful static charge, and it goes to ground through the first thing the cable touches.

12
00:00:40.975 --> 00:00:42.750
Don’t let that be you.

13
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.800
Never tie the hoist cable to your boat.

14
00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:49.575
If the helicopter has to move, it must be free.

15
00:00:49.825 --> 00:00:56.625
And keep everyone in life jackets, with a light, a flare or a signal mirror ready to show them where you are.
